The proposed methodology is validated using three standard IEEE benchmark distribution systems.

IEEE 33-Bus Distribution System
•	Small-scale radial distribution network 
•	33 buses 
•	Used for validating optimization performance 
•	Suitable for comparing convergence characteristics 
•	
IEEE 69-Bus Distribution System
•	Medium-scale benchmark system 
•	More switching combinations 
•	Used for evaluating robustness and optimization capability
•	 
IEEE 118-Bus Distribution System
•	Large-scale practical distribution network 
•	High computational complexity 
•	Used to evaluate scalability and computational efficiency of BOA 
These benchmark systems are widely used in power system research for evaluating Distribution Network Reconfiguration algorithms.
